{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moshe went up.</b> As HaShem said to him, 'go up to the mountain of the Avarim' — even so, he delayed going up until he had blessed them first." "<b>Mount Nevo.</b> It is the mountain of the Avarim; it is the top of the peak." "<b>Nevo.</b> It was in the portion of Reuven, as it is written, 'and the children of Reuven built Cheshbon' etc., 'and Nevo, and Baal Meon.' And what is written regarding Gad — 'for there the portions of the lawgiver are hidden' (ספון)' — one may say that Nevo was on the border, between the inheritance of Reuven and Gad." "<b>Et all the land.</b> Moshe saw with his eyes what Yehoshua did not walk with his feet, for there remained of the land of Israel that which he did not conquer and distribute in his lifetime to the tribes, as is explicit in the book of Yehoshua." "<b>Et the Gilad.</b> From the Gilad, which was across the Jordan to the east. The sun was where Moshe stood in it." "<b>As far as Dan.</b> For it is the border of the land of Israel, as it is written: מדן באר שבע (from Dan to Beersheba)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:35.730715441Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}